Appendix – Summary of Developer Clarifications (TradingHub Q&A Integration)

(for Front Running v2 & Market Risk Influence Logic)

During the validation process, several technical questions were raised to TradingHub regarding the schematic logic and key mathematical components of the Front-Running V2 (Over-Facilitation) and Market-Risk-Influence (MRI) frameworks. Their responses were reviewed and incorporated into the model understanding. Key clarifications are summarised below.

1. Market Risk Influence (MRI) – Interpretation and Parameter Behaviour

Developer Clarification Summary:

MRI is designed to map the market risk of a principal position into an equivalent USD-value that offsets the raw Narrative score.

MRI values lie in the range [0,1], where:

MRI → 1 indicates high market risk: model penalises the Narrative more heavily.

MRI → 0 indicates low market risk: little penalisation.

Default MRI = 0.5 reflects SME judgement and academic evidence related to investor risk aversion.

MRI is customer-configurable, but extreme values require TradingHub approval, as MRI strongly alters alert outcomes.

How to include in your report:

TradingHub clarified that the MRI parameter is intended to temper the Narrative score by incorporating market-risk exposure. MRI scales the Narrative into USD terms and prevents false positives in high-risk environments. The default of 0.5 reflects empirical judgement but is tunable subject to governance.

