3. Role of Sensitivities in Narrative vs. Counter-Narrative

Developer Clarification Summary:

Sensitivities appear in two parts of the model:

Expected market impact calculations (GMM output).

Risk-based penalties in Counter-Narrative.

Sensitivities indicate how much each trade is exposed to the underlying risk factors, thus affecting both potential benefit (Narrative) and potential cost (Counter-Narrative).

How to include in your report:

Sensitivities are used twice in the model: first to quantify market-impact gain (Narrative) and again to estimate principal-risk exposure (Counter-Narrative). This ensures the model differentiates between profitable abuse and legitimate risk-taking.

