5. “Cost of P With/Without Facilitation F” – Mathematical Interpretation

Developer Clarification Summary:

Linear MIM uses the price difference immediately before/after a trade.

MIMv2 uses an integral of trade impact due to concavity.

“Cost of P with facilitation F” = cost of unwinding principal after facilitation trades have shifted market memory.

“Cost of P without facilitation F” = theoretical cost of unwinding assuming client trades never occurred.

Narrative = advantage gained from facilitation trades.

How to include in your report:

TradingHub clarified that the cost calculations rely on the market-impact model’s memory terms. Facilitation trades shift the memory, generating a more favourable exit price for the principal position. The Narrative equals this differential benefit.

